M194F_INDEPENDENT_INPUT {"evidence":{"counts":[2,2,2,2,2],"first_pass":"manual decode companion; separate failed arm below uses the real fold","hooks":10,"sites":374},"name":"actual-confidence-second-decode-valid","pass":true}
frames          : 5 from M194F-NO-RAW-DIRECTORY  (first decode 0.00 s)
planes          : 32 x 24 per CFA plane
analysis domain : 22 x 17 at full-plane origin (5, 4) -- Crop is applied BEFORE luma, variance, weighting and accumulation
--- the merge ---
bands           : 1 Laplacian levels + 1 base, coarsest 11 x 9
selection       : SOFT -- weight = (band power above the noise floor)^exponent, a convex combination.
                  Sign coherence is free: a convex combination cannot take adjacent
                  coefficients from opposite-signed frames, which is the ringing a
                  coefficient-wise argmax produces.
noise gate      : 2.00 x the modelled band-noise power. Below it, NO frame may win and the
                  merge averages -- which is the correct estimator when there is no
                  information, and the only operation that gets below single-frame noise.
exponent        : 2.00
per-band exp    : 2   (coarsest -> finest)
                  sharpness ramps 1.4x per octave toward the fine bands. A wrong pick in a
                  fine band is one high-frequency coefficient nobody can see; a wrong pick
                  in a coarse band IS the rim.
base band       : plain mean across frames
not applied     : photometric gain, clip census, outlier rejection, halo correction, through-focus
                  statistics. Those are the --merge estimator path's stages; this arm is the merge only.
coverage mode   : crop -- as asked, --cover
alignment       : ON (M194f supplied identity), reference frame 2, 5 placed / 0 refused, 0.0 s
  held-out err  : NOT MEASURED   resampler: CatmullRom
  coverage      : CROPPED to the region EVERY frame covers -- 22 x 17 plane px at (5, 4) of 32 x 24, emitted at UNITY SCALE. 27.3% of width dropped and NOT upsampled (k=0.7273), so the output is SMALLER than the plane by design and no placement carries a coverage scale. The reference frame's own placement reaches the gather unmodified.
memory plan     : 5 canonical chunks, 1 reusable frame worker, 1 retained + 1 scratch accumulator, 2 execution threads
                  CONSTANT in the frame count and reduction order. Chunks run serially; spatial work uses
                  the execution pool. STREHL_PYRAMID_WORKERS=N changes threads, never arithmetic.

folded          : 5 / 5 frames in 0.1 s (0.02 s per frame, 2 execution threads)
band noise gain : 0.8894 0.0748
                  (E[L_k^2] / sigma_0^2, MEASURED on these operators, not derived.)
averaged        : 0.0% 100.0%
                  per level, the fraction of coefficients where NO frame cleared the noise
                  floor and the merge therefore averaged instead of selecting. Near 0%
                  everywhere would mean the gate is not gating and this is a naive
                  pyramid stacker.

